// A docs board for the pattern page Run on a schedule every N ticks. The Source has a timer, not a
// webhook: every 60 ticks it makes an item on its own. A belt carries each item into a Factory,
// whose code is the scheduled job: it counts its runs in ctx.state and emits a report. A second
// belt carries each report to a Debug Sink, which logs it. The run makes no outbound call.
//
//   row 2:   SOURCE 0 (timer, every 60 ticks) -b3-> FACTORY 1 -b4-> SINK 2
//
// The script is empty: the timer alone drives the board. It comes due on ticks 60, 120, 180 and
// 240, and the Source puts out an item on the tick after each.
//
// The Factory's Fault port stays undocked. The code never throws, so nothing faults.
//
// Handles mint in command order: the Source 0, the Factory 1, the Sink 2, then the belts 3 and 4.
// The 11 commands and the history seal end the boot on tick 12.
//
// machine_kind u8 legend: SOURCE=0, FACTORY=2, SINK=7. Dock `port` is the catalog port index:
// SOURCE Out=0; FACTORY In=0, Out=1, Fault=2; SINK In=0. In the code, ctx.emit(0, ...) sends on
// the Factory's first output, catalog port 1.
//
// Format 2 adds two fields a page reads and the core never does: `title`, the name a page shows,
// and `captions`, the ticks a viewer pauses on, each with the machine it highlights and one
// sentence about what the board does on that tick.
Board(
    format: 2,
    title: "Run on a schedule every N ticks",
    seed: 97,
    commands: [
        Place(kind: 0, cell_x: 1, cell_y: 2),        // 0: SOURCE, set to a timer below
        Place(kind: 2, cell_x: 5, cell_y: 1),        // 1: FACTORY In (5,2) Out (7,2)
        Place(kind: 7, cell_x: 11, cell_y: 2),       // 2: SINK, Debug
        DrawBelt(cells: [(2, 2), (3, 2), (4, 2)]),   // 3
        DrawBelt(cells: [(8, 2), (9, 2), (10, 2)]),  // 4
        Dock(belt: 3, endpoint: Tail, node: 0, port: 0),
        Dock(belt: 3, endpoint: Head, node: 1, port: 0),
        Dock(belt: 4, endpoint: Tail, node: 1, port: 1),
        Dock(belt: 4, endpoint: Head, node: 2, port: 0),
        Configure(node: 0, config: Source(trigger: Timer(interval_ticks: 60))),
        Configure(node: 1, config: Factory(source: r#"// the scheduled job: count the runs, report
export default function (input, ctx) {
  const runs = (ctx.state.runs || 0) + 1;
  ctx.state.runs = runs;
  ctx.emit(0, { job: "report", run: runs });
}"#)),
    ],
    script: [],
    captions: [
        // Measured: h0 Source WORKING[61,121,181,241]; script empty.
        Caption(tick: 61, highlight: 0, text: "The Source makes an item on its own, with no webhook. Its timer comes due every 60 ticks, and each item starts the job."),
        // Measured: effect step_ends_on=105 DEBUG {"job":"report","run":1}; h1 Factory WORKING[83,...].
        Caption(tick: 105, highlight: 2, text: "The Debug Sink logs the first report, run 1, which the Factory made from the timer's item."),
        // Measured: h0 Source WORKING[...,121,...], 60 ticks after 61.
        Caption(tick: 121, highlight: 0, text: "The Source makes its next item, 60 ticks after the first. The Factory will count it as run 2."),
    ],
    executor: Executor(default: Reply(after_ticks: 1), rules: []),
    view: View(fit: Board),
    end_tick: 300,
)
